questions.stem:
At a design critique, a student summarizes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {8, 11, 15, 16, 19, 24, 28, 33, 34};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 28) return steps; if (a[mid] < 28) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps; Which answer is correct for this case?

In a lab notebook entry, an engineer summarizes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {5, 0, -4, 9, 8, 0};
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) acc += a[i];
return acc;

Using the given data, answer this. What does this string routine return?
String s = "ioayc";
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++)
  if ("aeiou".indexOf(s.charAt(i)) >= 0) acc++;
return acc;

Using the given data, answer this. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {2, 6, 10, 14, 15, 16};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 12) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 12) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

During a team briefing, an engineer summarizes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(5);
Node b = new Node(35);
Node c = new Node(30);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

Analyze the following details. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {6, 8, 11, 16, 18, 21, 26, 30, 34, 39, 41};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 44) return steps; if (a[mid] < 44) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps;

Analyze the following details. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {6, 5, 6, 8, 3, 0, 3, 7, 1};
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) if (a[i] > 1) acc++;
return acc;

The case below gives the figures. Consider the following question. What does this string routine return?
String s = "eyabauii";
int acc = 0, target = 'a';
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) if (s.charAt(i) == target) acc++;
return acc;

On a work order, an engineer summarizes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Work out the answer to this item. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {-2, 0, 3, 6, 9, 12, 16, 20, 21};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 42) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 42) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

Review the following and respond. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(35);
Node b = new Node(20);
Node c = new Node(10);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;
